-- title:
--   Cyclic generator for the reduced Eisenstein socle at q
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be primes with $q \neq p$, and let $A_q$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$, in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the nonunits of $A_q$. Equip `JZero p`, the degree-zero Picard group of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the module structure `heckeModuleBar p` over `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ (the action through the Hecke operators when they commute, and the trivial substitution otherwise). Write $\mathfrak{P} =$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, the preimage under the algebra map `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal $(q) \subseteq \mathbb{Z}$, and let $\mathrm{red} =$ `reductionModL Aq p` be the reduction homomorphism from `JZero p` to `JZeroC (IsLocalRing.ResidueField Aq) p` attached to $A_q$ and its residue map. Then for all natural numbers $k$ and $M$ there exists $y_0$ in the submodule $V$ of elements of `JZero p` annihilated by the ideal generated by the constant $q^k$ together with $\mathfrak{P}^M$, such that $\mathrm{red}(g \cdot y_0) = 0$ for every $g \in \mathfrak{P}$, and such that every $y \in V$ with $\mathrm{red}(g \cdot y) = 0$ for all $g \in \mathfrak{P}$ satisfies $\mathrm{red}(y - m \cdot y_0) = 0$ for some natural number $m$.
--
--   This is the special-fibre part of Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein ideal: the $\mathfrak{P}$-socle of the image under reduction at $q$ of the $q^k$- and $\mathfrak{P}^M$-torsion of $J_0(p)$ is cyclic, exhibited here by an explicit generator modulo the kernel of reduction. It feeds the inertia-refined form of the same cyclicity statement and the resulting bound on the cardinality of the image of this torsion under reduction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_nsmul_generator_heckeTorsion_span_sup_of_reductionModL_eisensteinMaximalIdeal_smul_eq_zero.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_EisensteinIdeal
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Ramification
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ReductionModL

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
